  "id": "reproductive-type",
  "term": "reproductive type",
  "definition": "Reproductive type means the mode of reproduction an organism shows, such as producing males from unfertilized eggs and females from fertilized eggs, or producing females from unfertilized eggs. In this packet, it specifically refers to a form of thelytoky in which meiosis is absent, called apomictic thelytoky.",
